{
    "chapter_num": 20,
    "verses_count": 34,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Laborers in the Vineyard"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“For the kingdom of heaven is like a householder who went out early in the morning to hire laborers for his vineyard. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "After agreeing with the laborers for a denarius"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "The denarius was a day’s wage for a laborer"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " a day, he sent them into his vineyard. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And going out about the third hour he saw others standing idle in the market place; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and to them he said, ‘You go into the vineyard too, and whatever is right I will give you.’ So they went. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Going out again about the sixth hour and the ninth hour, he did the same. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And about the eleventh hour he went out and found others standing; and he said to them, ‘Why do you stand here idle all day?’ "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "They said to him, ‘Because no one has hired us.’ He said to them, ‘You go into the vineyard too.’ "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when evening came, the owner of the vineyard said to his steward, ‘Call the laborers and pay them their wages, beginning with the last, up to the first.’ "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when those hired about the eleventh hour came, each of them received a denarius. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now when the first came, they thought they would receive more; but each of them also received a denarius. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And on receiving it they grumbled at the householder, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "saying, ‘These last worked only one hour, and you have made them equal to us who have borne the burden of the day and the scorching heat.’ "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But he replied to one of them, ‘Friend, I am doing you no wrong; did you not agree with me for a denarius? "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Take what belongs to you, and go; I choose to give to this last as I give to you. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Am I not allowed to do what I choose with what belongs to me? Or do you begrudge my generosity?’"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or is your eye evil because I am good?"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So the last will be first, and the first last.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "A Third Time Jesus Foretells His Death and Resurrection"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And as Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, he took the twelve disciples aside, and on the way he said to them, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "“Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man will be delivered to the chief priests and scribes, and they will condemn him to death, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and deliver him to the Gentiles to be mocked and scourged and crucified, and he will be raised on the third day.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Request of the Mother of James and John"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then the mother of the sons of Zeb′edee came up to him, with her sons, and kneeling before him she asked him for something. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to her, “What do you want?” She said to him, “Command that these two sons of mine may sit, one at your right hand and one at your left, in your kingdom.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Jesus answered, “You do not know what you are asking. Are you able to drink the cup that I am to drink?” They said to him, “We are able.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He said to them, “You will drink my cup, but to sit at my right hand and at my left is not mine to grant, but it is for those for whom it has been prepared by my Father.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when the ten heard it, they were indignant at the two brothers. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But Jesus called them to him and said, “You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and their great men exercise authority over them. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "It shall not be so among you; but whoever would be great among you must be your servant, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and whoever would be first among you must be your slave; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 28,
                    "num_str": "28",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "even as the Son of man came not to be served but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jesus Heals Two Blind Men"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 29,
                    "num_str": "29",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And as they went out of Jericho, a great crowd followed him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 30,
                    "num_str": "30",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And behold, two blind men sitting by the roadside, when they heard that Jesus was passing by, cried out,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities insert Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " “Have mercy on us, Son of David!” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 31,
                    "num_str": "31",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The crowd rebuked them, telling them to be silent; but they cried out the more, “Lord, have mercy on us, Son of David!” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 32,
                    "num_str": "32",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jesus stopped and called them, saying, “What do you want me to do for you?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 33,
                    "num_str": "33",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "They said to him, “Lord, let our eyes be opened.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 34,
                    "num_str": "34",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And Jesus in pity touched their eyes, and immediately they received their sight and followed him."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}